Description: Route swaybar pointer input like i3bar
 Status scripts written for i3bar don't behave the same under swaybar:
 clicks between status blocks fire bar bindings or switch workspaces,
 blocks without a name never report clicks, `bindsym button1 nop` in the
 bar block doesn't stop workspace clicks, a `--release` binding stays
 silent after a workspace click, and click events carry no output_x or
 output_y, so a script can't place a popup next to the clicked block.
 .
 With click events enabled, the status line now owns its area, from the
 first block to the end of the bar: separators, gaps and edge padding
 swallow presses and wheel steps. Blocks without a name report clicks
 (without "name"), and a block's clickable area includes its borders and
 min_width padding. A press binding replaces a workspace button's
 built-in action; a release binding runs on top of it. Click events
 report x and y in the global layout plus output_x and output_y relative
 to the bar's output, measured from where the bar surface really sits
 (found through a throwaway xdg_popup, falling back to the gaps).
 swaybar-protocol(7) documents the new fields.
 .
 Backport of the change sent upstream, adapted to 04-dbus-tray: it reuses
 that patch's xdg_wm_base binding (adding the ping listener) and its
 hotspot callback arguments (seat, serial).
